mpi4pyscf 0.4.0
---------------
Bind to pyscf>=2.5, mpi4py>=4.0, Python>=3.13  (tested with pyscf-2.13.0,
mpi4py-4.1.2, Open MPI 4.1.6, Python 3.13, numpy 2.5)
* Bugfix
  - Deadlock on all worker ranks at the end of mpi.work_share_partition (used
    by CCSD(T)) on Python>=3.3.  The worker event loop runs inside the import
    of mpi4pyscf, and a helper thread unpickling mpi.Message blocked forever
    on the package's import lock.
  - NameError in CCSD(T) kernel and in the full-vvvv CCSD path
    (process_clock/perf_counter), undefined _mo_without_core, and a typo in
    CCSD.gather_amplitudes
  - MP2 on workers failed with PySCF>=2.x (no _scf object on workers)
  - lib.diis.restore referenced an undefined name; numpy.linalg.linalg no
    longer exists in numpy 2
* Changed
  - Removed the distutils-based version check (distutils is gone in Python
    3.12). pyscf>=2.5 is now required
  - Warn at startup if the MPI library does not provide MPI_THREAD_MULTIPLE
  - tests/conftest.py lets pytest be started on every rank
    (mpiexec -np N pytest tests) without an INTERNALERROR on the workers
  - Tests compare to serial PySCF instead of hardcoded energies; added tests
    for CCSD/CCSD(T) and the mpi4pyscf.tools.mpi communication helpers
* PBC (mpi4pyscf.pbc.df)
  - FFTDF and AFTDF work with pyscf-2.13 and are tested against serial PySCF
  - Fixed: AFTDF exchange at k-points was multiplied by the number of ranks
    (pyscf's new algorithm does not use the prange hook); complex densities
    in FFTDF.get_j; get_nuc/get_pp return shape for kpts=None (pyscf>=2.10);
    G=0 exchange treatment follows the installed pyscf (changed in 2.13);
    kpts is a property in pyscf>=2.x and was not synchronized to the workers
  - FFTDF/AFTDF.get_jk now default to exxdiv=None, as in PySCF
  - DF (GDF) works with pyscf-2.13: 1D/2D/3D, Gamma point and k-points,
    kpts_band, get_eri/ao2mo, loop; tested against serial PySCF. It always
    uses the compensated-charge algorithm, independent of the process count.
    DF.get_pp/get_nuc are PySCF's own and run on the master process
  - DF class no longer inherits the MPI AFTDF (GDF does not derive from AFTDF
    in PySCF 2.x); eta/mesh are estimated as in pyscf's _CCGDFBuilder;
    make_modrho_basis was called with eta instead of exp_to_discard;
    undefined name `member`
  - mpi.reduced_yield never streamed the workers' values to the master
    (workers are always in the running state), so DF.loop/AFTDF.loop in serial
    mode hung or lost data; building the integrals lazily from inside the
    returned generator broke the collective-call protocol
  - MDF is not ported yet and raises NotImplementedError
  - Added pbc/df/_compat.py (fuse_auxcell, auxbar, get_pp helpers, k-points)
* Known issues
  - PySCF's MPI (T) kernel (lib/cc/ccsd_t.c, MPICCget_wv) treats the
    occupied-virtual Fock term with t2 indices swapped relative to the serial
    kernel; about 1e-10 Eh in E(T) with default SCF settings

